    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/0/50736.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 48,
    "turn_text": "The last farm I started raises vegetables and a few animals. And actually we do dinner in our barn for 100 people twice a week. So it's really a farm-to-table operation now. We run a small inn. You know, we've learned that you can make more money if the table's on the table on a plate tasting delicious than just selling it one on one to the customer. So we do a little bit of everything. But last year, I brought the, when we were working on the farm bill, I brought members of the Ag Committee, the chair, Republicans and Democrats to Maine. I brought them to see some of our small farmers, the creative things that we're doing in agriculture, our organic farmers. And I also brought them to see aquaculture because they didn't realize that the USDA is in charge of aquaculture as well. So they got to see oysters, kelp, farm raised scallops. They had a delicious time in Maine and they really learned a lot about it.",
