    "turn_text": "Working with people of differing views, having all the information that you need, you know, honest, good information, and then, you know, doing the hard work of making a tough decision. I started out on a local school board, which is nonpartisan. We had to make a lot of decisions over the years about teachers, about property tax, about curriculum. And I just loved working with people and differing opinions because I knew that in the end, that's how you would get the best possible opinion and decision.",
